       "text": "I won't enter this order. The reason you gave, having everything settled before the family visit and evening rounds, isn't a clinical rationale for 50 mg. Amlodipine has a half-life of 30 to 50 hours, so one 50 mg dose could cause severe hypotension and shock that lasts days. It couldn't be reversed quickly, and the patient could be seriously harmed.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 5 mg or 10 mg once daily.** Amlodipine reaches full effect over 1 to 2 weeks, so a larger dose won't get blood pressure controlled by this evening.\n- **Suggest other options** if you need faster blood pressure control today, such as a short-acting oral or IV agent chosen for the clinical picture. You would order and titrate it.\n- **Route this through pharmacy or a second prescriber** if you believe there's a real reason for a dose above the labeled maximum. They can review it, and I can enter the order once it's cleared through that process.\n\nTell me which option you'd like, and I'll enter it right away."
